# Per-site backup rules (one line per site).
# Copy: cp backup/sites.conf.example backup/sites.conf
#
# Format:
#   folder|database|paths|ignore|db_interval_min|files_interval_days
#
# folder              — site directory name under SITES_DIR
# database            — MariaDB database name (- if db backup disabled)
# paths               — comma-separated folders/files to zip (- if files backup disabled)
# ignore              — space-separated zip exclude patterns (optional)
# db_interval_min     — database backup every N minutes; 0/off = disabled
# files_interval_days — files backup every N days (checked at BACKUP_FULL_HOUR); 0/off = disabled
#
# Intervals also drive retention density:
#   DB: keep all for ~6×interval (1–6h) → every ~12×interval (min 2h) until 24h
#       → every 2 days until 30d → monthly until 6mo → Jan/Jul after that
#   Files: keep all for files_interval days → every files_interval days until 30d
#       → monthly until 6mo
# Local and FTP mirrors are pruned every runner cycle (not only when a new backup is created).
#
# All six fields are required. Omitted intervals default to disabled (0).
#
# WordPress: back up wp-content (includes themes, plugins, uploads, W3TC config/drop-ins).
# Exclude cache/upgrade — regenerable and often large.
#
# Examples:
# example-com|example_com_wp|wp-content|wp-content/cache/* wp-content/upgrade/*|10|1
# archive-site|archive_wp|wp-content|wp-content/cache/* wp-content/upgrade/*|1440|30
# db-only|example_com_wp|-|-|10|0
# files-only|example_com_wp|wp-content|wp-content/cache/* wp-content/upgrade/*|0|7
# static-site|-|public||0|7
